{"at": "2026-11-11T02:58:19Z", "class": ["lesson"], "evidence": ["review:sha256-58ffb153514a"], "id": "2ac30862a4870ca0", "kind": "note", "scope": "global", "session": "4b868782-889f-5bca-a001-51649d97bcef", "text": "A named, matching template ties a plain brief on pass and costs more tokens on every task (CB-211: 8/8 vs 8/8, +63% tokens); keep the plain brief as default and name a template only when its extra care (characterisation tests, down paths, row accounting) is wanted", "trust": "observed"}
{"at": "2026-11-11T02:58:19Z", "class": ["lesson"], "evidence": ["review:sha256-5d06fc3c3290"], "id": "315396f78688dee5", "kind": "note", "scope": "global", "session": "4b868782-889f-5bca-a001-51649d97bcef", "text": "Never pipe a test run into tail inside an && chain: the pipe's exit status hides failures, and a commit went through on a red suite (CB-211)", "trust": "observed"}
{"at": "2026-11-11T02:58:19Z", "class": ["lesson"], "evidence": ["review:sha256-4f5847e42753"], "id": "5600c999237d760e", "kind": "note", "scope": "global", "session": "4b868782-889f-5bca-a001-51649d97bcef", "text": "In paired runs give each arm a distinct task text: hr hire supersedes this session's open contract for the same task", "trust": "observed"}
